# Brazilian Lemonade

Status: Untested

## Recipe Name:
Brazilian Lemonade (Brazilian Limeade)

## Servings:
6

## Prep Time:
5 minutes

## Cook Time:
None

## Ingredients:
- 4 juicy limes, washed and scrubbed
- 6 cups (1.4 L) cold water
- 1 cup (200 g) granulated sugar
- 6 tablespoons (90 ml) sweetened condensed milk
- Ice, for serving
- Thin lime slices, for garnish

Use limes with thin, smooth skin. They have less white pith, and the pith is where the bitterness comes from. Do not purée the limes. Pulse only a few times.

## Instructions:
1. Wash the limes thoroughly with a little hand or dish soap to remove wax and pesticides. Slice off the ends of each lime, then cut the limes into eighths.
2. Put half of the water, half of the sugar, and half of the limes in a blender. Pulse 5 to 7 times. Do not blend until smooth.
3. Pour the mixture through a fine-mesh strainer into a large pitcher. Press the pulp with the back of a spoon to release the juice. Discard the skins and pulp. Repeat with the remaining water, sugar, and limes.
4. Stir in the sweetened condensed milk. Taste. If the drink is at all bitter, stir in a little more condensed milk or sugar.
5. Serve over lots of ice with thin lime slices. Drink it the same day; it does not keep well.

Source: Amy Nash, "Easy Brazilian Lemonade (Limeade)". House of Nash Eats. https://houseofnasheats.com/brazilian-lemonade-limeade/

